[0.321, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H     \u001b[2m 37 \u001b[22m the shell: every hook does nothing by default, so a game overrides only what it needs, and the\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 38 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mshell with no game is the engine with nothing of a game in it. A program's `main` passes its \u001b[48;2;92;2;0mgame\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m      \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m 39 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mto `RunRenderApplication` ([a program's main](app-shell.md#a-programs-main)); the hooks the ground     \r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m3\u001b[9G +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mshell\u001b[17Gwith\u001b[22Gno\u001b[25Ggame\u001b[30Gis\u001b[33Gthe\u001b[37Gengine\u001b[44Gwith\u001b[49Gnothing\u001b[57Gof\u001b[60Ga\u001b[62Ggame\u001b[67Gin\u001b[70Git.\u001b[74GA\u001b[76Gprogram's\u001b[86G`main`\u001b[93Gpasses\u001b[100Gits\u001b[104G\u001b[48;2;4;71;0mworld and\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m39 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\u001b[48;2;4;71;0mits game \u001b[48;2;2;40;0mto\u001b[23G`RunRenderApplication`\u001b[46G([\u001b[38;2;230;219;116ma program's main\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m](app-shell.md#a-programs-main)); the hooks the gr\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m    +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mound                                                                                                   \r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m40 \u001b[22m sample\u001b[18Guses\u001b[23Gare\u001b[27Gin\u001b[30G[\u001b[38;2;230;219;116msamples\u001b[39m](sample-game.md#the-hooks-it-uses).\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m41 \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 42 \u001b[11G\u001b[22m##\u001b[14GChecking\u001b[23GManifest\u001b[32Gbefore\u001b[39Ga\u001b[41Gcapability\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ Yes, the game world must be a single source of truth. The GUI is as you say only for displaying the state of the \u001b[39m     \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mworld which is held and arbitrated by the server. The server is trusted, the client is considered unreliable and \u001b[39m     \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mmight be sending unsafe commands, so they all need checking on the server before they can be acted upon. A pre-check \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mon the client is just a formality to speed up time before informing the player the command has failed.\u001b[39m                \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mIs there value in splitting the assets and mods into client and server folders? What are the pros and cons?\u001b[39m           \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m✽\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;215;119;87mIonizing… \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m(7m 57s · ↓\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m42.4k tokens)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  Tip: Hit shift+tab to cycle between manual mode, auto-accept edit mode, and plan mode\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;136;136;136m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── jettison-0036 ─\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[39m\u001b[2mPress up to edit queued messages\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[38C\u001b[3B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m · esc to interrupt · ← 1 agent · ↓ to manage\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[21;3H\u001b[?25h"]
