[0.078, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[98C\u001b[26B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m8\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[21;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[0.016, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[2C\u001b[10B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mYes, the game world must be a single source of truth. The GUI is as you say only for displaying the state of the \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bworld which is held and arbitrated by the server. The server is trusted, the client is considered unreliable and \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bmight be sending unsafe commands, so they all need checking on the server before they can be acted upon. A pre-check \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bon the client is just a formality to speed up time before informing the player the command has failed.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BIs there value in splitting the assets and mods into client and server folders? What are the pros and cons?\r\u001b[36C\u001b[2B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m · \u001b[38;2;193;193;193mthinking with high effort\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m)\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[21;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[0.018, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[39C\u001b[16B\u001b[38;2;188;188;188mthinking with high effort\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[21;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[0.096, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[16B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m·\u001b[40G\u001b[38;2;183;183;183mthinking with high effort\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[21;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[0.027, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[109C\u001b[26B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m9\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[21;3H\u001b[?25h"]
