[0.939, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mCommitted \u001b[1m1600cae\u001b[22m, ran \u001b[1m8\u001b[22m shell commands · \u001b[38;2;255;107;128m3 failed\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mCommitted as \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m1600cae\u001b[39m. Running the gate in lane C; it waits its turn on the heavy lock if the L44 lane holds it.\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mRunning cd '/home/ivan/projects/jettison.lane-c/' && ./sc…\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  $ cd '/home/ivan/projects/jettison.lane-c/' && ./scripts/ci.sh --werror --asan --log build/gate.log (1m 0s · 2 \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Blines)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ AI should be handled by the server as only the server has the authority to make a lot of the decisions and changes an\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mAI will run. It's possible we also need to run some on the client which can make \"requests\" against the server.\u001b[39m       \r\u001b[1B                                                                                                                        \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mYou suggestions for the split are approved. One clarification, the server is handling physics, will the bake / cook \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mprocess bake out the collision meshes for models when those are available and the code is ready?\u001b[39m                      \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m*\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;235;159;127mIonizing…\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m(Run the full gate on J30 · 13m 0s · ↓\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m54.7k tokens)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  Tip: Hit shift+tab