[0.087, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mAI should be handled by the server as only the server has the authority to make a lot of the decisions and changes an\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mAI will run. It's possible we also need to run some on the client which can make \"requests\" against the server.\u001b[39m       \r\u001b[1B                                                                                                                        \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mYou suggestions for the split are approved. One clarification, the server is handling physics, will the bake / cook \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mprocess bake out the collision meshes for models when those are available and the code is ready?\u001b[39m                      \r\u001b[2B\u001b[49m  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mSearched for \u001b[1m2\u001b[22m patterns \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[39m Collision shapes will be baked by the cook into a world-content file that both client and server read, and J12 will\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  bake the same file through a small tool until the cook exists. I'm holding off on editing lane C while its gate runs,\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  and the approved split goes onto the roadmap once it passes.\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m · summary\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[53C\u001b[6B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m6\u001b[56G6\u001b[68Gthought for 10s)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[21;3H\u001b[?25h"]
