[0.125, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 186 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mruns left, as a crash leaves them (one named for a process that runs is another writer's, and         \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 187 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mkept). The partial file is made anew with the permissions the caller gives, 0644 unless told otherwise\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m 188 \u001b[22m (`Core::kFilePermissions`), so a file a game keeps private, such as a server's secret key at 0600,\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 189 \u001b[22m is never open to others on its way. Why both flushes are needed is\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 190 \u001b[22m [\u001b[38;2;230;219;116mdecided\u001b[39m](decisions.md#persistence). On failure it throws\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(~/projects/jettison.lane-b/docs/persistence.md)\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mAdded\u001b[12G\u001b[1m1\u001b[22m line, rem\u001b[24Gved \u001b[1m4\u001b[30G\u001b[22mlines\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m196\u001b[12G\u001b[22m`RENAME_NOREPLACE`\u001b[31G(Linux;\u001b[39Gthe\u001b[43Gone\u001b[47Gcall\u001b[52Gis\u001b[55Gin\u001b[58G`core/src/File.cpp`),\u001b[80Gso\u001b[83Gthere\u001b[89Gis\u001b[92Gno\u001b[95Gcheck\u001b[101Gfor\u001b[105Ganother\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m197\u001b[12G\u001b[22mwriter to\u001b[22Gcom\u001b[26G between: of two\u001b[43Gwrit\u001b[48Grs making the sam\u001b[66G file one leav\u001b[81Gs it whole and t\u001b[98Ge other gets\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 198 \u001b[12G\u001b[22m`Core::FileExistsError`,\u001b[37Ga\u001b[39G`std::runtime_error`\u001b[60Gnaming\u001b[67Gthe\u001b[71Gpath,\u001b[77Gwith\u001b[82Gits\u001b[86Gpartial\u001b[94Gfile\u001b[99Gremoved.\u001b[108GA\u001b[110Gfile\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 199 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242malready there is as it was, a directory in the way included. \u001b[48;2;92;2;0mIts\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m \u001b[48;2;92;2;0mpartial \u001b[48;2;61;1;0mfile \u001b[48;2;92;2;0mis\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m \u001b[48;2;92;2;0mnamed\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m \u001b[48;2;92;2;0mfor\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m \u001b[48;2;92;2;0mits\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m \u001b[48;2;92;2;0mwriter\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m,\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m 200 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m`<name>:partial.<process ID>.<count>`, since two writers of one file at once would otherwise write    \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 201 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242minto the same partial and one could rename the other's half-written bytes into place. A crash leaves  \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m 202 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mthat partial behind, and nothing removes it. The file system must support the flag (ext4, xfs, btrfs  \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 199 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242malready there is as it was, a directory in the way included. \u001b[48;2;4;71;0mThe\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m file \u001b[48;2;4;71;0msystem\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m \u001b[48;2;4;71;0mmust\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m \u001b[48;2;4;71;0msupport\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m \u001b[48;2;4;71;0mthe\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m \u001b[48;2;4;71;0mflag (ex\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m\u001b[48;2;4;71;0mt4\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m,\u001b[48;2;4;71;0m xfs, btrfs\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m                                                                                        \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[2m 200 \u001b[22m and tmpfs do); on one that does not, the write throws naming the path and the reason.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 201 \r\u001b[1B\u001b[22m \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m 202 \u001b[12G\u001b[22mA missing directory is made by `Co\u001b[77Go\u001b[79Gtermost\u001b[87Gfirst, each\u001b[99Gon\u001b[102G's parent\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[0.276, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 182 \u001b[22m 3. It is renamed over the target.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 183 \u001b[22m 4. The directory is flushed, since the rename is an entry in the directory.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(~/proj\u001b[17Gcts/jettis\u001b[28Gn.lane-b/docs/persistence.md)\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mAdded\u001b[12G\u001b[1m3\u001b[22m lines, removed \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m line\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 182 \u001b[12G\u001b[22m3.\u001b[15GIt\u001b[18Gis\u001b[21Grenamed\u001b[29Gover\u001b[34Gthe\u001b[38Gtarget.\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m 183 \u001b[22m 4. The dir\u001b[23Gc\u001b[25Gory is flushed, since th\u001b[50G r\u001b[53Gname\u001b[58Gis\u001b[61Gan\u001b[64Gentry\u001b[70Gin\u001b[73Gthe\u001b[77Gdirectory.\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[2m 184 \u001b[12G\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 185 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mThe partial file is made anew with the permissions the caller gives, 0644 unless told otherwise       \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 185 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mBefore it writes, it removes the partial files of the same target that a writer which no longer       \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 186 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mruns left, as a crash leaves them (one named for a process that runs is another writer's, and         \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 187 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mkept). The partial file is made anew with the permissions the caller gives, 0644 unless told otherwise\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m 188 \u001b[22m (`Core::kFilePermissions`), so a file a game keeps private, such as a server's secret key at 0600,\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 189 \u001b[22m is never open to others on its way. Why both flushes are needed is\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 190 \u001b[22m [\u001b[38;2;230;219;116mdecided\u001b[39m](decisions.md#persistence). On failure it throws\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(~/projects/jettison.lane-b/docs/persistence.md)\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mAdded\u001b[12G\u001b[1m1\u001b[22m line, rem\u001b[24Gved \u001b[1m4\u001b[30G\u001b[22mlines\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m196\u001b[12G\u001b[22m`RENAME_NOREPLACE`\u001b[31G(Linux;\u001b[39Gthe\u001b[43Gone\u001b[47Gcall\u001b[52Gis\u001b[55Gin\u001b[58G`core/src/File.cpp`),\u001b[80Gso\u001b[83Gthere\u001b[89Gis\u001b[92Gno\u001b[95Gcheck\u001b[101Gfor\u001b[105Ganother\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m197\u001b[12G\u001b[22mwriter to\u001b[22Gcom\u001b[26G between: of two\u001b[43Gwrit\u001b[76Gleav\u001b[81Gs it whole and t\u001b[98Ge other gets\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[0.215, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m74\u001b[12G\u001b[22mA save reported written must survive\u001b[49Ga\u001b[51Gcrash\u001b[57Gor\u001b[60Ga\u001b[62Gpower\u001b[68Gcut\u001b[72Gthat\u001b[77Gfollows\u001b[85Git.\u001b[89GSaves,\u001b[96Gsettings\u001b[105Gand\u001b[109Gthe\r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m75\u001b[12G\u001b[22mmod list are all\u001b[29Gwritten whole through\u001b[51G`Core::WriteFileDurably` (`core/File.h`):\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 176 \r\u001b[1B\u001b[22m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 177 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m1. The bytes go to a partial file beside the target, \u001b[48;2;92;2;0m`<name>:partial`.\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m \u001b[48;2;92;2;0mThe\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m \u001b[48;2;92;2;0mcolon makes it a name no\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m   \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 178 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m   virtual path can have, so nothing reads it as content.                                             \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 177 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m1. The bytes go to a partial file beside the target, \u001b[48;2;4;71;0mthe\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m \u001b[48;2;4;71;0mwrite's\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m \u001b[48;2;4;71;0mown,\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m                                 \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 178 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m   `<name>:partial.<process ID>.<count>`. The colon makes it a name no virtual path can have, so      \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 179 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m   nothing reads it as content; the writer's own name means two writers of one file at once never     \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 180 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m   write into one partial, where one could rename the other's half-written bytes into place.          \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m 181 \u001b[22m 2. The partial file is flushed to the disk (`fsync`).\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 182 \u001b[22m 3. It is renamed over the target.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 183 \u001b[22m 4. The directory is flushed, since the rename is an entry in the directory.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(~/proj\u001b[17Gcts/jettis\u001b[28Gn.lane-b/docs/persistence.md)\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mAdded\u001b[12G\u001b[1m3\u001b[22m lines, removed \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m line\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 182 \u001b[12G\u001b[22m3.\u001b[15GIt\u001b[18Gis\u001b[21Grenamed\u001b[29Gover\u001b[34Gthe\u001b[38Gtarget.\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m 183 \u001b[22m 4. The dir\u001b[23Gc\u001b[25Gory is flushed, since th\u001b[50G r\u001b[53Gname\u001b[58Gis\u001b[61Gan\u001b[64Gentry\u001b[70Gin\u001b[73Gthe\u001b[77Gdirectory.\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[2m 184 \u001b[12G\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 185 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mThe partial file is made anew with the permissions the caller gives, 0644 unless told otherwise       \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 185 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mBefore it writes, it removes the pa\u001b[76Gt that a writer which no longer       \u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
